# CWYD-2 — health endpoints. Run against `docker compose up --build --wait`
# (VS Code / Cursor REST Client, or JetBrains HTTP Client).

# From inside the dev container the published ports live on the host daemon
# (docker-outside-of-docker): set @host = host.docker.internal there.
@host = localhost
@api = http://{{host}}:8000
@web = http://{{host}}:8080

### Liveness: 200 {"status":"ok"}; never touches the database
GET {{api}}/health

### Readiness: 200 {"status":"ready","pgvector":"0.8.7"}
# 503 {"detail":"database unavailable"} after `docker compose stop db`
GET {{api}}/health/ready

### Same API through the frontend's nginx proxy (/api prefix stripped): 200 {"status":"ok"}
GET {{web}}/api/health

### Readiness through the proxy: 200 {"status":"ready","pgvector":"0.8.7"}
GET {{web}}/api/health/ready

### SPA: 200 text/html with <title>Chat With Your Docs</title>, also for unknown routes
GET {{web}}/documents/123
